# The project OS parses YAML frontmatter, domain manifests, and case manifests
# with exact line-ending assumptions, and the generated status/registry files are
# content-hashed. A default Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) used to turn
# every docs/domains and docs/contracts page into CRLF, which silently broke
# `node tools/vibe.mjs doctor`, `context`, `verify`, and `status`.
#
# Keep text files LF in the working tree on every platform instead of relying on
# the local core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated Emscripten bundles are stored exactly as the toolchain emits them and
# are byte-compared by the cooker artefact tests; never normalise them.
# Emscripten may emit end-of-line spaces; preserve exact build bytes rather than
# rewriting generated modules to satisfy source whitespace checks.
OEngine/src/assets/web-cook/wasm/vendor/** -text whitespace=-blank-at-eol

# Binary assets and build outputs must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.ico binary
*.glb binary
*.wasm binary
*.oegpack binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.a binary
*.lib binary
*.bin binary
*.zip binary
